        "original_id": "eee6e6ac-499e-5a25-8108-eb3a5d94d255",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dorothy Parker, Maxine Kumin, Leonard Bernstein, John Latouche, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, Eugene Lee\n- Works: Candide, Sweeney Todd, Wicked\n- Roles: poet, author, critic, satirist, designer\n- Awards: Tony Awards, Drama Desk Award\n\nFacts:\n- Dorothy Parker was born on August 22, 1893, and she was an American poet, short story writer, critic, and satirist known for her wit, wisecracks, and observations of 20th-century urban foibles.\n- Maxine Kumin was born on June 6, 1925, and she was an American poet and author.\n- Dorothy Parker was one of several contributors to the text of Candide, along with John Latouche, Lillian Hellman, Stephen Sondheim, John Mauceri, John Wells, and Leonard Bernstein.\n- Eugene Lee won Tony Awards for Bernstein’s Candide, Sondheim’s Sweeney Todd, and Wicked.\n- Eugene Lee also won the Drama Desk Award for Outstanding Set Design.\n- Dorothy Parker died on June 7, 1967.\n- Maxine Kumin died on February 6, 2014.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
